      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You have hit on a critical ethical risk: conflation of cultural norms with behavioral risk can lead to discriminatory underwriting that assumes certain lifestyles are inherently less stable than others. Modern regulatory frameworks generally prohibit this by requiring insurers to distinguish between actual behavioral variance and cultural differences that are statistically neutral or positive in their own context. To avoid penalizing culture, your model should explicitly whitelist specific cultural indicators (like community involvement) as stability factors rather than treating them as noise, while ensuring data classes are diverse enough to represent all communities fairly.",
